{
  "name": "Error starter · 1 Sync records",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Error starter · Sync records\nReads a list of records from an API, reads each record, and saves it to a data table.\n\n**Fetch records**: Settings > Retry On Fail, 3 tries, 1000 ms apart. On Error is left at \"Stop Workflow\": if all 3 tries fail, the run fails and the error workflow is called (Workflow settings > Error workflow).\n\n**Fetch one record**: Settings > On Error = \"Continue (using error output)\". A record that cannot be read leaves by the lower output and is saved with status `failed`. The other records go on. The run ends green and the error workflow is NOT called. Retry On Fail is off here on purpose: together with the error output it only retried when the first item failed (see README). The next run tries the record again.\n\n**Save record / Save as failed**: Upsert with `record_id` as the condition. A second run updates the same rows; it does not add rows.",
        "width": 900,
        "height": 350,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "ddf189bc-7eca-445b-86ec-53c193dc13e8",
      "name": "About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -440
      ]
    },
